invariant: INV-38
file: tls_write.c
catches: diff
builds: bin/diff
reason: records_fill pays the overhead of the whole records and not of the
  last record, so when cap ends in part of a record, ch_writable_len
  answers up to 22 bytes more plaintext than cap holds. The Lean theorems
  bound spec/lean/Spec/TlsWrite.lean's model by cap, and the model no
  longer computes what the C computes, so test/diff_writable_len.h's rows
  object: the proofs would be about code that no longer ships.

--- old
    size_t overhead = (whole + 1) * REC_OVERHEAD;
--- new
    size_t overhead = whole * REC_OVERHEAD;
